{
  "version": 1,
  "scope": {
    "modeled": [
      "L_ibx",
      "L_stg",
      "L_net"
    ],
    "note": "Client-to-host direction only. Host-to-client *Result types are authored by the host, so they disclose nothing the host did not already have. This file records what an untrusted host can OBSERVE; it is not an integrity model, so who may forge a field is out of scope except for the `signed` annotation.",
    "excludedSurfaces": [
      {
        "surface": "group_outbox_do",
        "reason": "Group chat is outside the package scope of the write-up; these entries would have no table row to map to, which would hollow out the unmapped-is-a-failure rule."
      },
      {
        "surface": "device_registry_do",
        "reason": "Device registration and runtime-auth state. Host-visible and real, but the write-up models the inbox and storage components; these entries would have no table row to map to, which would hollow out the unmapped-is-a-failure rule. Enumerating it is its own work."
      }
    ],
    "excludedRoutePrefixes": [
      "/v1/groups/",
      "/v1/group-invite/",
      "/v2/runtime/",
      "/v2/runtime-auth/"
    ],
    "internalPathMatchers": [
      "services/cloudflare/src/inbox/durable.ts",
      "services/cloudflare/src/group-outbox/durable.ts",
      "services/cloudflare/src/device-registry/durable.ts"
    ],
    "nonSyntacticLeakage": [
      {
        "channel": "record_count_per_device",
        "checked": false
      },
      {
        "channel": "ciphertext_length",
        "checked": false
      },
      {
        "channel": "inter_arrival_timing",
        "checked": false
      },
      {
        "channel": "commit_frequency",
        "checked": false,
        "note": "Doubled by the R1 rotation change; recorded there as a traffic-pattern cost. Also directly readable today from PrivateMessage.content_type and epoch; after the R3 wrap only size class remains."
      },
      {
        "channel": "mls_frame_header_epoch_and_content_type",
        "checked": false,
        "note": "PrivateMessage.epoch and content_type are cleartext in every frame and identical at both inboxes; not a sentinel so not caught by Check X. Removed by the R3 frame wrap."
      },
      {
        "channel": "retention_window",
        "checked": false,
        "note": "Records are deleted only at retention expiry, not on ack, so the host holds every envelope header for 30 days past delivery."
      },
      {
        "channel": "source_ip_and_tls_fingerprint",
        "checked": false,
        "note": "Already carried by the Linkability row as `sender address`. The network layer is not addressable here, so application-layer anonymity is the ceiling of any repair in this component."
      }
    ],
    "limits": [
      "Containment is not information. This checks for a sentinel SUBSTRING, so any leak that is a FUNCTION of a secret - a hash, a size bucket, a first byte, a few bits of tag - passes clean. Consequence worth stating plainly: if conversation_id is ever 'fixed' by hashing it, these checks go quiet while the leak may be unchanged.",
      "Non-syntactic channels are not modelled at all; see nonSyntacticLeakage, where checked:false records that their absence is a decision and not an oversight.",
      "`table` is not reconciled against the write-up. CI proves a human recorded a placement, not that the table contains that row. Closing this needs the table vendored into the repo.",
      "Inhabitation (bits) is declared, not yet measured. `constant` and `absent` claims are reviewed by hand until an engine-driven corpus check lands; the structural path set and the carries sets ARE measured.",
      "Compile-time exhaustiveness has holes: serde(flatten), a serde_json::Value-typed field, serde(untagged), or a non-exhaustive match elsewhere would each make these checks go quiet rather than red. None are present in the in-scope types today."
    ]
  },
  "tables": {
    "sender_identity": "tab:inbox, Social graph rows",
    "message_index": "tab:inbox, Linkability rows",
    "envelope_metadata": "tab:inbox, Timing and Traffic type rows",
    "attachment_refs": "tab:inbox, storage-ref rows (new; not in the table as published)",
    "non_repudiation": "tab:inbox, Non-repudiation row",
    "transport_addressing": "L_net, request-line addressing",
    "storage_namespaces": "L_stg, object key namespaces",
    "unmapped": "NO DECISION RECORDED - this value fails CI",
    "inbox_state_keys": "tab:inbox, inbox-side state keys (new; not in the table as published)",
    "realtime_push": "tab:inbox, Receiver behaviour rows"
  },
  "sentinels": {
    "literal": [
      "plaintext_body",
      "group_title",
      "display_name",
      "attachment_file_name"
    ],
    "captured": [
      "sender_user",
      "recipient_user",
      "sender_device",
      "recipient_device",
      "message_nonce"
    ]
  },
  "inlineCiphertext": {
    "mls_application": "opaque",
    "mls_commit": "opaque",
    "mls_welcome": "opaque",
    "control_contact_removed": "base64_json_snake",
    "control_contact_accepted": "base64_json_snake",
    "control_group_welcome_pickup": "base64_json_camel",
    "control_device_membership_changed": "base64_ascii"
  },
